{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob066_edgecapture",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input  clk\r\n - input  reset\r\n - input  in    (32 bits)\r\n - output out   (32 bits)\r\n\r\nThe module should examine each bit in the 32-bit input vector, and\r\ncapture when the input signal changes from 1 in one clock cycle to 0 the\r\nnext. \"Capture\" means that the output will remain 1 until the register is\r\nreset (active high synchronous reset). Assume all sequential logic is\r\ntriggered on the positive edge of the clock.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "clk",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "reset",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "in",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 32,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "out",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 32,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, single self-contained TopModule DUT; xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "31dc42e7-0efc-4874-9a0b-588c82bffef8",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "42299500-49ce-4328-a031-f3ab6ea959ce",
    "source_sha256": "19931ac47ebec9fe67ad13b023ede4ae9ee68c639b71aef3e9dcedeb78d4f00f",
    "source": "\nmodule TopModule (\n    input  logic        clk,\n    input  logic        reset,\n    input  logic [31:0] in,\n    output logic [31:0] out\n);\n    logic [31:0] prev;\n\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (reset) begin\n            prev <= 32'b0;\n            out  <= 32'b0;\n        end else begin\n            out  <= out | (prev & ~in);\n            prev <= in;\n        end\n    end\nendmodule\n"
  },
